Resource-binding invariance
===========================

Let q and q' be byte encodings of requests. The adapter compares every raw
root field except bounded_resource_budget byte for byte. In particular the
parents array, Root_import reference, scientific role and mode are equal.
The complete Root_import and the numerical manifest are also identical.
The prepared records agree outside request, gate and budget references.
The gates agree outside request and budget. The budgets agree outside two
SDK destination rows and the literal request/gate command paths; every cap,
profile, policy, mathematical Source, caller and old Source/control reference
is equal. Hence the new child has the same Original mathematical input and
method, while its exact operational command and provenance are new.

This equality does not prove that the new child succeeds. A later genuine
Root invocation, exact guard/result/whole-input check and distinct actual
review are still necessary. It also does not assert that the failed v1 ran
a mathematical computation: its genuine traceback and fixed base Source
identify a failure before Popen, joined to Root's separately scoped current
absence observation and historical prelaunch freshness evidence. The new
record preserves that history as guard setup failure, not resource refusal.

The borrowed metadata operations receive a separately admitted context.
Their old function bodies are whole-byte exact, but the named context and
three adapters are new Source: cohort/base admission, effective preparation
and metadata API identity. Phase outputs name the supplement. Registration
retains both preparation identities and the transition inside the actual
records; administrative checks compare those records canonically and retain
all prior values byte for byte. These are conditional metadata statements,
not a new group-theoretic proof, case verdict, whole-level result or credit.
